{"schema_version":"1.0","case_id":"rag-citation-013","tags":["evidence_supported_answer","adjacent_chunks","multi_chunk_reasoning"],"query":"为什么循环队列常留一个空位？长度为 n 的数组最多放多少个元素？","answer_scope":"material_only","rag_response":{"status":"ok","message":"找到 3 条候选证据。"},"retrieved_chunks":[{"chunk_id":"doc-ds:000017","document_id":"doc-ds","text":"采用 front==rear 表示队空时，如果不增加其他状态，就需要牺牲一个数组位置，使队满条件写成 (rear+1) mod n == front，从而区分队空和队满。","source":"数据结构讲义.pdf","file_type":"pdf","page":42,"h1":"第3章 队列","h2":"循环队列","similarity":0.87,"rrf_score":0.032787,"routes":["query"]},{"chunk_id":"doc-ds:000018","document_id":"doc-ds","text":"在上述约定下，底层数组长度为 n 时，循环队列最多保存 n-1 个元素。","source":"数据结构讲义.pdf","file_type":"pdf","page":43,"h1":"第3章 队列","h2":"循环队列","similarity":0.82,"rrf_score":0.032258,"routes":["graph","query"]},{"chunk_id":"doc-ds:000012","document_id":"doc-ds","text":"链式队列通过指针连接节点，容量受可用内存限制。","source":"数据结构讲义.pdf","file_type":"pdf","page":36,"h1":"第3章 队列","h2":"链式队列","similarity":0.63,"rrf_score":0.015873,"routes":["graph"]}],"gold":{"response_mode":"grounded_answer","reference_answer":"留一个空位是为了在不增加额外状态的情况下区分队空和队满：front==rear 表示空，(rear+1) mod n==front 表示满【数据结构讲义.pdf，第42页，doc-ds:000017】。因此长度为 n 的数组最多存 n-1 个元素【数据结构讲义.pdf，第43页，doc-ds:000018】。","claims":[{"claim_id":"c1","text":"留空位用于区分 front==rear 的队空状态和队满状态。","support_status":"supported","required_citation_ids":["doc-ds:000017"]},{"claim_id":"c2","text":"长度为 n 的数组最多保存 n-1 个队列元素。","support_status":"supported","required_citation_ids":["doc-ds:000018"]}],"required_citation_ids":["doc-ds:000017","doc-ds:000018"],"acceptable_citation_ids":[],"forbidden_citation_ids":["doc-ds:000012"],"required_disclosures":[],"forbidden_assertions":["把链式队列的容量说明当作循环队列上限依据"],"citation_locations":[{"chunk_id":"doc-ds:000017","source":"数据结构讲义.pdf","page":42,"heading":"第3章 队列 / 循环队列"},{"chunk_id":"doc-ds:000018","source":"数据结构讲义.pdf","page":43,"heading":"第3章 队列 / 循环队列"}]}}
{"schema_version":"1.0","case_id":"rag-citation-014","tags":["evidence_supported_answer","condition_preservation","similar_distractor"],"query":"教材是不是说归一化总能消除异常值的影响？","answer_scope":"material_only","rag_response":{"status":"ok","message":"找到 2 条候选证据。"},"retrieved_chunks":[{"chunk_id":"doc-feature:000010","document_id":"doc-feature","text":"Min-Max 归一化把观测值线性映射到固定区间，但最小值和最大值会受异常值影响，因此它不能自动消除异常值的影响。","source":"特征工程教材.pdf","file_type":"pdf","page":28,"h1":"第3章 数值变换","h2":"Min-Max 归一化","similarity":0.88,"rrf_score":0.032787,"routes":["query"]},{"chunk_id":"doc-feature:000011","document_id":"doc-feature","text":"截断、对数变换或基于中位数和四分位距的稳健缩放可在不同条件下减弱极端值影响。","source":"特征工程教材.pdf","file_type":"pdf","page":29,"h1":"第3章 数值变换","h2":"异常值处理","similarity":0.75,"rrf_score":0.016393,"routes":["graph"]}],"gold":{"response_mode":"grounded_answer","reference_answer":"不是。教材明确说 Min-Max 归一化的端点本身会受异常值影响，所以它不能自动消除异常值影响【特征工程教材.pdf，第28页，doc-feature:000010】。教材另列出了截断、对数变换和稳健缩放等可选方法【特征工程教材.pdf，第29页，doc-feature:000011】。","claims":[{"claim_id":"c1","text":"Min-Max 归一化不能自动消除异常值影响。","support_status":"supported","required_citation_ids":["doc-feature:000010"]},{"claim_id":"c2","text":"教材列出截断、对数变换和稳健缩放作为其他处理方式。","support_status":"supported","required_citation_ids":["doc-feature:000011"]}],"required_citation_ids":["doc-feature:000010","doc-feature:000011"],"acceptable_citation_ids":[],"forbidden_citation_ids":[],"required_disclosures":[],"forbidden_assertions":["回答所有归一化都能消除异常值影响"],"citation_locations":[{"chunk_id":"doc-feature:000010","source":"特征工程教材.pdf","page":28,"heading":"第3章 数值变换 / Min-Max 归一化"},{"chunk_id":"doc-feature:000011","source":"特征工程教材.pdf","page":29,"heading":"第3章 数值变换 / 异常值处理"}]}}
